Problem Statement

1. Title

AI-Powered Public Infrastructure Issue Reporting System

---

2. Domain

CivicTech / Smart City / Artificial Intelligence

The project focuses on using technology to improve the way citizens report and track public infrastructure problems. It combines a civic issue management platform with an AI-based image classification enhancement.

---

3. Who is the User?

3.1 Citizen

The Citizen is the primary user who can report public infrastructure problems such as:

- Potholes
- Damaged roads
- Broken streetlights
- Garbage accumulation
- Water leakage
- Other public infrastructure issues

The citizen can register, log in, submit an issue with a description, photograph and location, and track the status of the submitted complaint.

3.2 Municipal Officer

The Municipal Officer is responsible for handling reported infrastructure issues.

The officer can:

- View assigned complaints
- Verify reported issues
- View issue photographs and locations
- Update complaint status
- Add resolution details
- Mark issues as resolved

3.3 Administrator

The Administrator manages and monitors the overall application.

The administrator can:

- Manage users
- Manage issue categories
- Manage departments
- Assign issues to officers
- Monitor all reported issues
- View issue statistics
- Manage the overall system

---

4. What Problem Are We Solving?

Citizens frequently encounter public infrastructure problems such as potholes, damaged roads, broken streetlights, garbage accumulation and water leakage. However, they may not know the appropriate department or process for reporting these issues.

Traditional complaint processes may also make it difficult for citizens to know whether their complaint has been received, verified, assigned to an officer, or resolved. This can result in delayed reporting, poor visibility and difficulty in tracking the progress of complaints.

For example, when a citizen notices a large pothole on a busy road, they can use this application to upload a photograph, provide a description and capture the location of the issue. The system records the complaint and makes it available to the appropriate authority for verification, assignment and resolution.

The proposed system provides a centralized platform where citizens can report infrastructure issues and authorities can efficiently manage, track and resolve them.

---

5. Proposed Solution

The proposed system is a web-based AI-Powered Public Infrastructure Issue Reporting System that provides a centralized platform for reporting, tracking and managing public infrastructure issues.

5.1 Citizen Module

The citizen module will provide:

- User registration
- Secure login
- Infrastructure issue reporting
- Issue description
- Photograph upload
- Location capture
- Issue category selection
- View submitted complaints
- View complaint details
- Track complaint status
- View complaint history
- Receive status notifications

5.2 Officer Module

The officer module will provide:

- Secure officer login
- View assigned issues
- View issue details
- View uploaded photographs
- View issue location
- Verify reported complaints
- Update issue status
- Add resolution details
- Mark issues as resolved

5.3 Administrator Module

The administrator module will provide:

- Secure admin login
- User management
- Officer management
- Issue category management
- Department management
- Issue assignment
- Monitoring of all complaints
- Dashboard statistics
- Complaint status monitoring

5.4 Issue Tracking

Each reported issue will have a lifecycle that can be tracked.

Example:

Reported → Verified → Assigned → In Progress → Resolved

The system will maintain the status history of an issue so that the progress from reporting to resolution can be tracked.

5.5 Location Management

The system will store the location of reported infrastructure issues using location information such as coordinates and address details.

This allows officers to identify where the issue occurred and handle the complaint appropriately.

5.6 Notification Module

The system will provide notifications when important complaint events occur, such as:

- Issue submitted
- Issue verified
- Issue assigned
- Issue status updated
- Issue resolved

5.7 Dashboard and Statistics

The administrator will have a dashboard to monitor the overall system.

The dashboard can display:

- Total reported issues
- Pending issues
- Verified issues
- Assigned issues
- Issues in progress
- Resolved issues
- Issues by category
- Issues by department

5.8 AI-Based Issue Classification — Enhancement Feature

As the enhancement feature, the system will use an AI-based image classification approach to analyze an uploaded infrastructure issue photograph and suggest an appropriate issue category.

For example:

Uploaded Image → AI Analysis → Pothole Detected → Pothole Category Suggested

Possible categories may include:

- Pothole
- Road Damage
- Broken Streetlight
- Garbage
- Water Leakage
- Other

The citizen can review the suggested category before submitting the complaint.

The AI enhancement will be implemented during the later enhancement phase of the capstone rather than making the initial MVP dependent on AI.

