6. Core Entities / Database Tables

The system will contain the following core database entities:

1. User

Stores information about registered citizens, officers and administrators.

2. Role

Stores user roles and permissions such as Citizen, Officer and Administrator.

3. Issue

Stores the main infrastructure complaint details, including description, photograph, category, location and current status.

4. IssueCategory

Stores different types of infrastructure problems such as potholes, garbage, streetlight damage and road damage.

5. Department

Stores departments responsible for handling different categories of infrastructure issues.

6. Location

Stores the location information associated with a reported issue.

7. IssueAssignment

Stores the assignment of reported issues to responsible officers.

8. StatusHistory

Stores the historical status changes of each issue from reporting to resolution.

9. Notification

Stores notifications generated for users regarding complaint updates.

Main Relationships

- One Role can be associated with multiple Users.
- One Citizen can report multiple Issues.
- One Issue belongs to one IssueCategory.
- One Issue is associated with one Location.
- One Department can handle multiple Issues.
- One Issue can be assigned to an Officer.
- One Issue can have multiple StatusHistory records.
- One User can receive multiple Notifications.

The database design will contain real relationships between the entities rather than functioning as independent CRUD tables.

