8. Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful when the following criteria are achieved:

1. A citizen should be able to register and securely log in to the application.

2. A citizen should be able to submit an infrastructure complaint with a description, photograph, category and location in approximately two minutes.

3. A citizen should be able to view previously submitted complaints.

4. A citizen should be able to track the current status of each complaint.

5. An officer should be able to view and manage assigned complaints.

6. An officer should be able to verify complaints and update their status.

7. The system should maintain the complete status history of each complaint from reporting to resolution.

8. An administrator should be able to manage users, departments, categories and issue assignments.

9. The administrator should be able to monitor overall complaint statistics through a dashboard.

10. The application should provide a consistent REST API with appropriate authentication and authorization.

11. The application should be deployed on a public URL by Day 41 as required by the capstone guidelines.

12. The AI enhancement should analyze infrastructure issue photographs and provide a useful issue-category suggestion.

13. The system should maintain secure handling of passwords, authentication tokens and environment variables.

---

9. Out of Scope

The following features are outside the scope of this capstone project:

1. Direct integration with official government complaint management systems.

2. Automatic physical repair of roads, streetlights or other infrastructure.

3. Processing of real government payments.

4. Emergency response or emergency service management.

5. Real-time CCTV monitoring.

6. Real-time autonomous monitoring of every public infrastructure location.

7. Training a large AI model from scratch.

8. Deployment of physical IoT sensors throughout the city.

9. Automatic dispatch of physical repair teams without human verification.

10. Integration with confidential government databases or systems.

